title Caravan farewell -- the reader hears the plan's own last word
prompt Autonomous loop lap 545 -- Standfast on reds first, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; the last lap's recommend named the next rung of the correspondence arc as the constructive door, now that a rung costs three lines in one file plus its own step.
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md end to end -- every row from 1 to 100 is closed or released, the ledger scan reads verdict=ok at 5 rows and 23,991 bytes under its 24,576 bound, and the tree is clean at 1899f68b67. No agent-closable red stands, so the constructive queue opens honestly.
think Rota lap 545 mod 27 = 5 -- deep-read foundations/20260816-214652_standfast-the-stopped-line.md. Its three-part shape governed this whole lap: stop, root not symptom, prove then resume. It also names the lantern-becomes-a-loom rule, which is exactly what carried this round.
think The arc's honest next question, read off the rung below: refrain spares a reader and takes the summons down, and does both entirely inside the plan. From where that person sits the letters simply stop. A plan that honored their ending and a plan that lost their file read exactly alike from the outside, so the courtesy the whole arc was spent to earn arrives as an absence they must interpret.
think Named the rung under the Comlink tendency -- clearest, warmest, safest word. `farewell` is a plain word a newcomer grasps, sits beside `tidings.rye` as the arc's other outward-carrying noun, and greps clean across the tree (one MCP prompt fixture string and one line of nixos prose, no module). Rejected `bid` on the safety test: deemlow.com is a live-shopping surface and an auction sense would collide.
think Shaped it as beckon's mirror rather than refrain's. Beckon carries a wall outward to the reader's box; farewell carries the sparing outward the same way, fourteen bytes into caravan/.readers/desk.fares, so the plan publishes no second note of its own. The suffix is six characters like every other word in that box, held by a comptime assert against ".walls".
think Ordering: the record the rung below published must already stand before the letter goes out, since a letter announcing a sparing the plan has no record of would reach a person the plan cannot answer for. So the rung reads refrain_published first and never writes it -- and it runs before the refraining beneath it in the spine, reading that rung's record as the run before this one left it, exactly the wire-before-memory discipline every rung of this arc keeps.
think Fold D's promise came due and held. Adding the step to the arc was three lines plus an assert in the harness's `the_correspondence`, with no copy of anything beneath it. The rung's own new work was its section, its reader-box helpers, its step, its four checks, and its witness.
obs REDS %98's loom caught this lap's fault on its first pull, before a line of it reached a send. `farewell.rye`, born as a copy of `refrain.rye`, inherited all 39 of its delegations whole -- every one naming `respecting_rung`, two steps down, skipping its own neighbor -- and the copy meter read 47 carried lines climbing to 242. The reach guard named it exactly: `respecting_rung is folded into by more than one rung: farewell refrain`. Repointed one step down, the carry fell back to 47. This is a guard working, not a red: the class was booked, rooted, and walled in %98, and the wall did the whole job this time.
obs The carry standing at exactly 47 across a fifth birth is the round's honest proof. Fold C promised a rung would cost the ladder only its own new checks; the way to prove that is to add a rung and read the meter. 102 modules and 1,321 checks now, carry unmoved.
obs Four bodies lifted as the arc predicted they would. `check_refrain` and `check_refrain_refusals` became byte-identical across the two rungs the moment farewell was born, and `check_respect_measure` and `check_respect_wire` came with them since both now chain to the same place. Fold A climbs 913 to 952, fold B 85 to 89, and `check_refrain_measure` and `check_refrain_wire` take the terminal seat.
obs The lift ran through a transformer that reads string and comment spans before touching a token, so REDS %99's class could not recur -- the harness prose guard reads OK over 532 comments and 1,082 literals, and REDS %100's narrowed pattern welcomed every plain English "the rung below" in the lifted prose.
obs TAME's seventy-line ratchet fired on the one body this lap touched. `tell_beckon_own` had grown three lines a rung to 120 in farewell -- the printing staircase, a second instance of exactly the shape fold D just closed for orchestration. Answered where TAME asks, in the file being edited: split at the movement seams into three bodies of 34, 39, and 60 lines, so the new rung adds nothing past the bound. The elder rungs keep their 111 and 102 and turn on touch.
obs The printing staircase is the next crux this lap names in a number. It grows three lines a rung across every rung holding it, and the byte-identical meter cannot see it for the same reason it could not see the orchestration spine -- no two rungs hold the same body. A meter beside the spine meter, then a lift into the harness, is the shape the answer already has.
